{
  "id": "typescript-15-branded-and-opaque-types",
  "slug": "branded-and-opaque-types",
  "title": "Branded and opaque types for domain safety",
  "moduleId": "typescript-15-advanced-type-patterns",
  "order": 1,
  "hook": "**Branded types** add compile-time tags so `UserId` and `OrderId` are both strings at runtime but not interchangeable. Zero runtime cost — C# has nominal types natively.",
  "sections": [
    {
      "heading": "What is this?",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "text": "Brand: `type UserId = string & { readonly [__brand]: unique symbol }`. Factory validates then casts. **Opaque** hides structure — only factory constructs. Brands erase on emit — validation must be in factory."
        },
        {
          "type": "glossary",
          "title": "Key terms",
          "entries": [
            {
              "term": "brand",
              "longForm": "branded type",
              "plainDefinition": "Phantom tag on primitive.",
              "example": "string & { __brand: \"UserId\" }"
            },
            {
              "term": "opaque",
              "longForm": "hidden structure",
              "plainDefinition": "Consumers cannot see internals.",
              "example": "Opaque<string, \"Token\">"
            },
            {
              "term": "nominal",
              "longForm": "nominal typing",
              "plainDefinition": "TS structural — brands simulate nominal.",
              "example": "UserId ≠ OrderId"
            },
            {
              "term": "phantom",
              "longForm": "compile-time only",
              "plainDefinition": "Brand never at runtime.",
              "example": "erased on emit"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Why does it matter?",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "prose",
          "text": "Swap user/order IDs causes data bugs — brands catch compile-time. Currency cents vs dollars. UUID vs string."
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "variant": "tip",
          "title": "Interview trap: brand at runtime",
          "body": "Runtime still plain string — factory must validate."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "How it works step by step",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "steps",
          "title": "Mental model",
          "items": [
            {
              "title": "define brand",
              "body": "string & unique symbol"
            },
            {
              "title": "factory",
              "body": "validate + cast"
            },
            {
              "title": "API uses brand",
              "body": "loadUser(id: UserId)"
            },
            {
              "title": "ban export cast",
              "body": "as UserId only in factory"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "diagram",
          "diagram": {
            "type": "mermaid",
            "title": "Branded safety",
            "source": "flowchart LR\n  RAW[string] --> FACT[UserId()]\n  FACT --> API[loadUser]\n  RAW -.->|blocked| API"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "heading": "Code walkthrough",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "snippet",
          "snippet": {
            "language": "typescript",
            "label": "UserId vs OrderId",
            "code": "declare const __u: unique symbol;\ndeclare const __o: unique symbol;\ntype UserId = string & { readonly [__u]: never };\ntype OrderId = string & { readonly [__o]: never };\nfunction UserId(v: string): UserId { if (!/^usr_/.test(v)) throw new Error(); return v as UserId; }\nfunction loadUser(id: UserId) {}\nloadUser(\"ord_1\" as OrderId); // error",
            "explanation": "Distinct brands prevent swap."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "snippet",
          "snippet": {
            "language": "typescript",
            "label": "Cents branded",
            "code": "type Cents = number & { readonly __c: unique symbol };\nfunction Cents(n: number): Cents { if (!Number.isInteger(n)) throw new Error(); return n as Cents; }\nfunction add(a: Cents, b: Cents) { return Cents(a + b); }",
            "explanation": "Integer cents only."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "snippet",
          "snippet": {
            "language": "typescript",
            "label": "Opaque helper",
            "code": "type Opaque<T, Tag extends string> = T & { readonly __opaque: Tag };\ntype Token = Opaque<string, \"Token\">;\nfunction createToken(s: string): Token { if (s.length < 32) throw new Error(); return s as Token; }",
            "explanation": "Reusable opaque pattern."
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "snippet",
          "snippet": {
            "language": "typescript",
            "label": "Failure: cast bypass",
            "code": "const id = \"hack\" as UserId; loadUser(id); // compiles unsafely",
            "explanation": "as UserId without factory defeats brand."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
